{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/421963-r-i-p-leonard-nimoy","id":421963,"title":"R. I. P. Leonard Nimoy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-27T11:07:28-08:00","id":421963,"title":"R. I. P. Leonard Nimoy","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.foxnews.com/entertainment/2015/02/27/leonard-nimoy-spock-star-trek-dead-at-83/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2026/10/democracy26_navchip.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.foxnews.com/entertainment/2015/02/27/leonard-nimoy-spock-star-trek-dead-at-83/\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 | Fox News </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.foxnews.com/entertainment/2015/02/27/leonard-nimoy-spock-star-trek-dead-at-83/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.foxnews.com/entertainment/2015/02/27/leonard-nimoy-spock-star-trek-dead-at-83/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T12:15:17-08:00","id":422082,"title":"","content":"RIP<br /> <br /> :'(<br /> <br /> Ten characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T12:26:30-08:00","id":422105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonard Nimoy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A life is like a garden. Perfect moments can be had, but not preserved, except in memory. LLAP</div> </div> </div> </div>Nimoy's last ever Twitter post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T13:04:45-08:00","id":422139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonard Nimoy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A life is like a garden. Perfect moments can be had, but not preserved, except in memory. LLAP</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a beautiful quote for anyone, but for our particular H:tV troupe, it takes on a whole new meaning.<br /> <br /> See, one of the NPCs of our game was Sebastion, who was basically one of our &quot;commanding officers&quot; in our custom Conspiracy, if you will. He had a wonderful garden on top of our airship. During the biggest climax of our game thus far, we found out that he had been stuck in a time loop where somehow, some way, one of our characters would eventually go Slasher and slaughter the rest of us. He tried to prevent it from happening again and again, but always seemed to fail.<br /> <br /> Long story short, we found the entity that was responsible and took it down. We set things right and he was finally released from that torture. 2 weeks later we were all in the garden again when he asked us for a little bit of alone time. That was the last we saw of him.<br /> <br /> That was our latest session, so this tweet has such impeccable timing. I can't find the words to describe my incredible amounts of feels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T13:47:21-08:00","id":422191,"title":"","content":"As a nerd, Leonard Nimoy has had a bigger impact on my life and my outlook than most saints or prophets. I am grateful to him for his work, and I hope he finds reward in his rest. I also hope his family and friends are comforted in how many people share the weight of their loss, however distantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:41:56-08:00","id":422306,"title":"","content":"I was sad to hear thos today. And his last tweet was so perfect. He'll be greatly missed...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T21:56:06-08:00","id":422613,"title":"","content":"I can't say I've ever watched Star Trek or had any personal relationship with Nimoy or his characters. That said, the impact he has had on nerd culture is immense and obvious. He deserves nothing but the highest regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T01:36:10-08:00","id":422707,"title":"","content":"Leonard Nimoy talked me through the biblical landscape as a kid in such a compelling manner, that I, a kid who decided that if God truly existed he could only logically be genuinely evil or a complete idiot by age 8, sat down and read the entire Christian bible many times, and over the years, in many editions. He piqued an interest in mythology, morality and philosophy that led to a personal bexpansion of perspective that I didn't fully grasp until I was an adult.<br /> <br /> He also taught me that pointy ears looked cool on people, and that speaking intelligently (not that I know a Damn thing about true intelligence.) and being a reliably integral character can make you just as popular as punching lizard men and sleeping with green chicks can. And with a bit more class, too.<br /> <br /> You lived long, and you did prosper. I think the truest wish fans of yours have is that you could have just been given more time and prosperity. You deserved it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 02-28-2015, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T01:41:28-08:00","id":422714,"title":"","content":"When Spock died in Wrath of Kahn, they played this song. I don't know if it's appropriate or gauche, but I'm leaning toward appropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/euWfTiYwRB0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/euWfTiYwRB0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/euWfTiYwRB0\" target=\"_blank\"> http://youtu.be/euWfTiYwRB0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":1041,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","user":"brjedi26","date":". 02-28-2015, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T05:46:53-08:00","id":422835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/421963-r-i-p-leonard-nimoy?p=422714#post422714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it's appropriate or gauche, but I'm leaning toward appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, it's perfectly appropriate. Now, if you'd started wishes that he live long and prosper, I'd accuse you of being completely tone-deaf, but since there are so many other people doing it I'm glad to exclude you from the list.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T08:17:25-08:00","id":422946,"title":"","content":"While most known, of course, for being Spock, for *me* he'll always be the voice of &quot;In Search Of...&quot;, starting back in the 70's, when I was a kid. I saw that show before seeing repeats of Star Trek and recognized his voice when he was Spock, going &quot;Mom-- it's the voice-guy from the show...!&quot;. Regardless of when/where people first were exposed to him, Nimoy was a bannerhead for geek/nerd culture in all the positive ways imaginable. (Sidenote: I found his inclusion in the 2009 Trek movie more poignant and meaningful that Shatner's in '94's &quot;Generations&quot; -- Kirk may have been the &quot;face&quot; of Trek in geek culture, but Spock was its spirit... #PeaceAndLongLife )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T08:45:01-08:00","id":422967,"title":"","content":"COPD...*sigh*<br /> <br /> I remember the show &quot;In search of...&quot; and I never missed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:43:50-08:00","id":430268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/421963-r-i-p-leonard-nimoy?p=422714#post422714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Spock died in Wrath of Kahn, they played this song. I don't know if it's appropriate or gauche, but I'm leaning toward appropriate.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/euWfTiYwRB0\" target=\"_blank\">http://youtu.be/euWfTiYwRB0</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Along the same line the second thing I though when I heard the news was Kirk's recitation at the end of Wrath of Khan.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}